@description REAPER MCP — Model Context Protocol interface (immersive/spatial audio)
@version 1.9.0
@author James Livingston
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_mcp.dylib https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet/releases/download/v$version/reaper_mcp.dylib
@changelog
  Correctness release: 7.1.2 bed loudness, the identity-tone cache, and a routing
  detector that had been reporting false faults on 22.2. Surface UNCHANGED (190 tools /
  3 resources / 5 prompts) - this release adds one parameter and no verbs.
  analysis.verify_routing gave FALSE VERDICTS on 22.2. 22.2 is the only bed layout
  declaring two LFE slots, and the plan put the one 40 Hz LFE tone on both, so the tone set
  was not unique. A PERFECTLY ROUTED 24-channel render came back ok=false, with channel 3
  "bleed" at a margin of exactly 0.000000000 dB and channel 9 "duplicated", both at
  planCoverage 1.000000 - nothing in the numbers signalled it. Reaching it required doing
  exactly what the tool's own description instructs (passing back the echoed lfeChannels);
  with them omitted the same width read a clean 24/24, which is why it went unseen. The
  detector now REFUSES a degenerate plan outright and returns NO per-channel verdicts,
  rather than attaching a warning to a wrong answer.
  7.1.2 beds received NO BS.1770-4 channel weights, reading 0.350 LU LOW. bedChannelLabels()
  enumerated cases 1/2/6/8/12/16 with no case 10, while the LFE predicate beside it
  generalised - so a layout the product accepts silently lost its weights while reporting
  "multichannel". 7.1.2 is the default bedLayout in three spatial tool schemas, and the
  bed.expectLufs claim consumed by iamf-sentinel-pro's intent-compare inherited the error.
  spatial.inject_identity_tones advertised "7.1.2" in its own schema enum and then refused it
  at runtime. Every bed-layout width now derives from ONE canonical table; five hand-rolled
  per-consumer width mappings are deleted. A registry-walking guard asserts that every layout
  any tool advertises is accepted at runtime, so a tool written later is covered by default.
  spatial.inject_identity_tones served STALE AUDIO after a parameter change. Files were named
  by slot index alone, so two calls with different parameters shared one path; REAPER installs
  a per-path PCM cache on the second access, and from then on a rewrite of that path is
  invisible - the tool reported the parameters it was asked for while REAPER played the
  earlier audio. Filenames now carry a hash of the WAV bytes, so identical parameters still
  give identical paths (determinism holds, and the cache hit is then correct) while different
  parameters can no longer collide at all.
  NEW: spatial.inject_identity_tones gains constantHz - one frequency on every slot, LFE
  included, so a multichannel fixture can hold a single frequency. The 313 + 139k plan cannot
  express that. A plan carrying it is a level instrument, not a routing one, and the routing
  detector refuses it by construction.
